 "brief": "Israeli security and military institutions are preparing to significantly reduce troop levels in Gaza, the Shehab Wire reported, citing Hebrew Channel 14. The planned pullback would bring deployment levels closer to pre-operation numbers, though the report did not specify the scale of the reduction or the timeline for implementation.\n\nThe move marks a potential shift in Israel's military posture in the territory following months of intensive operations. The reduction would represent a major change in force composition in Gaza, though specifics about which units would be affected or when the withdrawal would begin remained unclear from the initial reporting.",
